comment_data.body:
'mini.surround' allows [buffer-local configuration](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-surround.html#module-setup) by setting a `vim.b.minisurround_config` variable. Its common usage is to customize surroundings per filetype.

My suggestion would be to put the following code (which is an adjusted version of [builtin `f` surrounding](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/9b935c218ddba02e5dc75c94f90143bce1f7c646/lua/mini/surround.lua#L1121-L1129)) in the '~/.config/nvim/after/ftplugin/plaintex.lua' (and/or other LaTeX adjacent filetype):

```lua
if _G.MiniSurround ~= nil then
  vim.b.minisurround_config = {
    custom_surroundings = {
      f = {
        input = { '\\%f[%w_%.][%w_%.]+%b{}', '^.-{().*()}$' },
        output = function()
          local fun_name = MiniSurround.user_input('Function name')
          if fun_name == nil then return nil end
          return { left = '\\' .. fun_name .. '{', right = '}' }
        end,
      },
    },
  }
end
```

